Make `enum wasmi_compilation_mode_enum` match the Rust implementation.

`wasmi/config.h` orders the values EAGER, LAZY, LAZY_TRANSLATION, but the Rust
`wasmi_compilation_mode_t` in `crates/c_api/src/config.rs` orders them EAGER,
LAZY_TRANSLATION, LAZY. A C caller passing WASMI_COMPILATION_MODE_LAZY_TRANSLATION
(1 in the header) therefore selected LAZY, and vice versa, so validation was
skipped when eager validation was requested. This reorders the header to match
the Rust values.

Present at wasmi v2.0.0 and still on upstream main (f0c20dc5).
Upstream: not yet reported

diff --git a/crates/c_api/include/wasmi/config.h b/crates/c_api/include/wasmi/config.h
index 67baa751..6da721f1 100644
--- a/crates/c_api/include/wasmi/config.h
+++ b/crates/c_api/include/wasmi/config.h
@@ -108,11 +108,11 @@ WASMI_CONFIG_PROP(void, floats, bool)
 enum wasmi_compilation_mode_enum {
   /// Wasmi compiles and validates Wasm bytecode eagerly.
   WASMI_COMPILATION_MODE_EAGER,
-  /// Wasmi compiles and validates Wasm bytecode upon first use.
-  WASMI_COMPILATION_MODE_LAZY,
   /// Wasmi compiles Wasm bytecode upon first use but validates Wasm bytecode
   /// eagerly.
   WASMI_COMPILATION_MODE_LAZY_TRANSLATION,
+  /// Wasmi compiles and validates Wasm bytecode upon first use.
+  WASMI_COMPILATION_MODE_LAZY,
 };
 
 /**
